Team,

Quick follow-up on the T-301 gauging routine. Since the recalibration
under WO-4012 and the weekly dips, the dip-vs-LT-304 difference has
stayed under 20 mm for eight straight weeks - well inside the 50 mm
action limit in SOP-U300-02.

Keep taking the closing dip after every receipt though. The IR-2025-032
event on T-101 started exactly this way: a transmitter that looked fine
because nobody cross-checked it while it was quietly stuck.

One observation: the dip hatch gasket is worn and the hatch doesn't seat
cleanly - I'll raise a low-priority work order so it gets picked up with
the next T-301 visit rather than becoming a vapour leak finding in an
audit.

Mary
